/code-review high 2026-10-09-kotlin-language-stack (branch at fdebe615)

1. plugins/vwf/skills/init/SKILL.md:356 — The new settings.gradle(.kts) and lone build.gradle(.kts) rows have no root-only guard like the *.xcodeproj row, so the stack read, which scans 'the root and every directory below it', picks up nested Android/included Gradle builds as separate kotlin projects. Failure: a Flutter app (pubspec.yaml plus android/settings.gradle.kts) or a React Native app in source mode: init proposes an extra android kotlin sub-project. Same for a build-logic/ included build. A plain Java build.gradle repo is also proposed as kotlin.
2. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/pack.yaml:22 — The pack declares lsp_servers key kotlin-lsp as `mise x -- kotlin-lsp --stdio`, but app-framework/flutter already declares the same key as `mise x kotlin@latest -- kotlin-lsp --stdio`. The machine-wide stackgen-lsp local plugin treats the same key with a different declaration as a conflict and does not write it. Failure: on a machine where a Flutter repo materialized first, a kotlin-library repo lands no Kotlin language server; the reverse order breaks the Flutter repo's.
3. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/templates/.config/mise/conf.d/kotlin/mise.toml:5 — version = "temurin-25" is the only non-latest, non-exact pin in any template, in a CI-loaded file. pinExact rewrites only latest and cmdUpgrade skips non-exact pins, so it is never made exact and never moved. Failure: builds are not reproducible; breaks tool-config's exact-pins-where-CI-loads rule; upgrade never reports a JDK row.
4. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/pack.yaml:21 — manifest: settings.gradle.kts is the file doctor's section 4 reads to check stack.frameworks and stack.dependencies, but a Gradle build declares dependencies in gradle/libs.versions.toml and each module's build.gradle.kts. Failure: every declared dependency token gets a 'declared but absent' drift finding; a Groovy settings.gradle repo has no manifest at all.
5. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/skills/kotlin/references/toolchain.md:21 — jvmToolchain(N) with N the oldest supported Java while mise installs only Temurin 25; Gradle toolchains need a JDK of exactly N, so the build fails or auto-downloads one outside mise. Temurin 25 cannot run Gradle wrappers older than 9.1. Failure: jvmToolchain(17) fails 'No matching toolchains found' on a mise-only machine or provisions via foojay; a Gradle 8.x wrapper fails under JDK 25.
6. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/audit/kotlin:33 — grype file:<lockfile> without --config .config/grype.yaml, so accepted ignores do not apply; per-file scans of settings-gradle.lockfile and buildscript-gradle.lockfile do not match syft's **/gradle.lockfile* cataloger glob; re-scans what code:sec's grype dir: already covers. Failure: accepted vulns reappear; settings lockfile reported audited with zero packages.
7. plugins/stackgen/stacks/bundles/kotlin-library.md:31 — says gradle.lockfile is 'written only by ./gradlew dependencies --write-locks', contradicting locking.md and the shipped stackgenResolveAll tasks. Failure: a user runs it in a multi-module build, module lockfiles are never written, the next --frozen CI run fails.
8. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/outdated/kotlin:16 — ./gradlew dependencyUpdates runs with no check the ben-manes plugin is applied; unknown task exits non-zero unlike every other missing-precondition path. Failure: setup:deps:outdated:all stops on a brownfield repo without the plugin.
9. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-gate/ktlint/config/.config/mise/tasks/code/format/ktlint:98 — without --fix, format runs exactly lint's command; with --fix, ktlint --format exits non-zero on any non-autocorrectable rule. Failure: double reports in CI; the format hook fails on lint violations.
10. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-gate/detekt/config/.config/mise/tasks/code/lint/detekt:29 — file discovery copy-pasted across three scripts; detekt uses git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree instead of the .git/GIT_DIR walk; install/upgrade duplicate the init-script printf block. Failure: under git's safe.directory refusal detekt silently falls back to find and lints untracked/gitignored files.
